Feature: The ground station gets the telemetry of the flight computer
  The ground station does not talk to ArduPilot. The MAVLink telemetry of ArduPilot goes to
  the flight computer. The flight computer sends it down the serial line to the TX15, and the
  TX15 passes it on. The link is narrow, so the flight computer cannot send more than the
  line carries. Its own frames for the TX15 go first.

  Expectation: The ground station hears the plane through the TX15
    Given the ground station telemetry is flowing
    When 5 seconds pass
    Then the ground station telemetry is flowing

  Expectation: The position on the map comes from the telemetry of the line
    Given the ground station telemetry is flowing
    And the ground station map distance is 400 m
    When 5 seconds pass
    Then the ground station map distance is at least 399 m
    And the ground station map distance is at most 401 m

  Expectation: Commands of the ground station reach ArduPilot
    Given the ground station telemetry is flowing
    When the ground station command is sent
    And 5 seconds pass
    Then the autopilot command is received

  Expectation: The telemetry does not use more than the line carries
    Given the ground station telemetry is flowing
    When 10 seconds pass
    Then the ground station telemetry rate is at most 4000 bytes per second

  Expectation: Without the TX15 the ground station hears nothing
    Given the ground station telemetry is flowing
    When the TX15 is not connected
    And 10 seconds pass
    Then the ground station telemetry is silent
